=== 3. BLIND SPOT PROVEN WITH THE PRE-WIDENING CODE ===========================
Two injections, both outside spec.assets, both silently accepted by every offline gate:
  examples/gltf-skin/assets/SimpleSkin_geometry.bin   168 B sha=35f0ca6bc07976c0 -> truncated to 0 B
  examples/gltf-viewer/assets/BoxTextured.glb        5956 B sha=b510eca2e2ef33f6 -> same-size garbage (sha=140f5c64dccb9476)
$ node tools/examples/spec-compliance-audit.cjs        → r7g-01-NOT-detected.log
  [spec-compliance] 45 examples: 0 fail / 1 warn   EXIT 0        ** NOT DETECTED **
The skinning geometry and an entire viewer model can be destroyed after capture and every offline gate stays
green. This is the F-38/F-39 class of hole one level deeper: the binding only covered what the spec chose
to name.

=== 4. CHANGE ================================================================
tools/verify/v11-spec-common.cjs
  new exported listAssetTree(exampleDir) — sorted POSIX-relative paths of every file under <example>/assets/**
  assetDigestsOf(exampleDir, assets) — scope is now  spec.assets ∪ listAssetTree  , each entry
    { path, declared, bytes, hash, present }  (declared flag added; ordering made deterministic)
tools/examples/spec-compliance-audit.cjs — S15 binding now iterates the union of (declared ∪ on-disk tree ∪
  paths present in the evidence record) so a file appearing on only one side is exactly what gets caught:
    declared & absent            -> S15-FREEZE   (unchanged message)
    bound & absent from disk     -> S15-ASSET-BIND "当期证据记录为 NB 实存文件，交付目录里已不存在"
    any zero-byte asset file     -> S15-FREEZE (declared) / S15-ASSET-ZERO (undeclared sidecar)
    present & not in evidence    -> S15-ASSET-BIND "（NB，assets/ 未声明边车）在当期证据中无内容哈希"
    bytes / sha256 mismatch      -> S15-ASSET-BIND (unchanged wording)
Deliberate non-choice: no field is added to example.json, because every spec.assets edit would move
specFingerprint and mass-invalidate otherwise valid evidence. Widening happens in producer + offline consumer.
Cost measured: 65 files / 4.9 MB sha256 per full capture run — negligible.

