=== 8. CAPTURE-TIME BEHAVIOUR — WHY S15-ASSET-ZERO EXISTS (NC-E6/NC-E7) =======
Probe A: break the asset BEFORE the browser run (gltf-skin, declared 1 / shipped 6)
  $ node tools/verify/v11-examples-verify.cjs --ids=gltf-skin
  FAIL gltf-skin {no-runtime-error, animation-playing, frame-diff, visible-frame, resource-released}
  0 promoted. The digest honestly recorded the empty file (bytes:0, hash e3b0c44298fc1c14 = sha256 of nothing).
  -> for this example class a broken sidecar cannot buy a PASS record.
Probe B: break a NON-required file of a catalog example (gltf-viewer, ui-shell contract, 50 files)
  assets/AnimatedMorphCube.glb truncated 6752 B -> 0 B, then re-run
  PASS gltf-viewer, validatorResults all 7 PASS (scene-ready/node-exists/asset-loaded/material-property/
  no-runtime-error/visible-frame/resource-released) — the example loads a different model, so its own
  contract stays green while one delivered asset is empty.
  -> an offline assertion is still required. With the new S15-ASSET-ZERO rule both directions fire:
     NC-E7a disk 0 B + record 0 B -> [FAIL] gltf-viewer S15-ASSET-ZERO: … 为 0 字节 …  EXIT 1  DETECTED
     NC-E7b disk restored, record still says 0 B -> [FAIL] … 当期证据记录为 0 字节（捕获当刻即为空资产）  DETECTED
     (observed as "3 fail / 1 warn" in the run; the 3rd was gltf-skin's S11-NO-EVIDENCE because a capture-time
      FAIL record legitimately overrides the older PASS record — the gate refusing to forget a failure.)
Residual, unchanged by this work: digests are taken from the same working tree as the run, so an asset whose
content was ALREADY wrong (but non-empty) at capture time cannot be proven correct offline. That needs upstream
provenance (R1 license/origin work), not a hash. Recorded as F-52, non-blocking.

