=== 8b. PRE-CAPTURE (PROVENANCE) TAMPER — the case a self-reported hash cannot see ===
The delivery carries its own upstream digests: examples/gltf-viewer/assets/SHA256.json (9 entries,
keys are bare file names relative to that manifest) and examples/gltf-viewer/assets/official/manifest.json
(16 entries, {name,file,revision,url,sha256,bytes}). All 25 agree with the bytes on disk today.
Consumer change: where such a manifest names a file, the offline gate compares the full sha256 against
the UPSTREAM value too, not only against the evidence record (new rule S15-ASSET-PROVENANCE).
NC-E8 (script: replace 5956 B BoxTextured.glb with same-size garbage BEFORE any capture, then capture):
  manifest expects b510eca2e2ef33f6, disk before tamper b510eca2e2ef33f6 (agreement=true)
  tampered to 140f5c64dccb9476 (identical 5956 B)
  $ node tools/verify/v11-examples-verify.cjs --ids=gltf-viewer
    CAPTURE EXIT 1 :: FAIL gltf-viewer {material-property,resource-released} — 0 promoted
    (so unlike the 0-byte case of §8, the browser contract does reject a garbage model: an empty file is
     skipped by the loader, a corrupt one is not. Both are covered: NC-E7a offline, NC-E8 both layers.)
  $ node tools/examples/spec-compliance-audit.cjs → r7g-08-NC-E8-gate-output.log
    [FAIL] gltf-viewer S15-ASSET-PROVENANCE: §15：assets/BoxTextured.glb 内容哈希 140f5c64dccb9476 ≠
           交付自带出处清单记载的 b510eca2e2ef33f6（资产在产证之前即已被替换，实物与证据一同失真）
    [FAIL] gltf-viewer S11-NO-EVIDENCE: status=stable 但当期证据 result=FAIL
    45 examples: 2 fail / 1 warn, EXIT 1   DETECTED
  Restored from scratch backup: 5956 B sha=b510eca2e2ef33f6 == upstream, re-captured, gate back to 0 fail / 1 warn.
Provenance coverage measured over the delivery: 25 of 65 asset files (38.5%) have an offline-verifiable
upstream digest, all in gltf-viewer; the other 7 examples ship no manifest. Extending it (a shared or
per-example SHA256.json, or embedding the digest in the spec) is a content decision for the owning team,
recorded as F-52's minimal fix rather than done here.

